# Profile mechanical-0.1 (Core 0.4 Stage D-1, LABS-1.023). Additive vocabulary only (D-D-1, D-D-9): installed after the
# full core with WorldModel.install_profile("mechanical"). Assemblies and components use core part-of; part kinds,
# materials, joint kinds and the assembly/component categories are vocabulary (D-D-11: "component" is a category, not
# a kind). Dependency kinds are core (core-0.4-d).
define
# A mechanical connection between two parts (symmetric: both are endpoints), optionally of a joint kind (a category:
# bolted, pressed, splined). Distinct from part-of (parthood) and from depends-on (dependency).
relation connected-to sub proposition, relates endpoint @card(2..2), relates joint-kind @card(0..1);
physical-object plays connected-to:endpoint;
category plays connected-to:joint-kind;
# A replacement: the removed part is the event's patient (specialised once, D-D-6); the fitted part has a role of its
# own, because in TypeDB 3.14.1 a second specialisation of `patient` would share its @card(0..1). A replacement is an
# event description: its acceptance never establishes that the replacement occurred.
relation replacement sub event, relates removed as patient, relates fitted;
physical-object plays replacement:removed, plays replacement:fitted;
